+### `StreamingResponse` { #streamingresponse }
+
+Takes an async generator or a normal generator/iterator and streams the response body.
+
+In recent FastAPI versions you can also **yield chunks directly from a path operation** when using `response_class=StreamingResponse`. FastAPI streams each chunk without JSON conversion:
+
+```python
+from collections.abc import Iterator
+
+from fastapi import FastAPI
+from fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse
+
+app = FastAPI()
+
+@app.get("/stream", response_class=StreamingResponse)
+def stream() -> Iterator[bytes]:
+    yield b"first\n"
+    yield b"second\n"
+```
+
+Use a synchronous generator when reading blocking file objects, or an async generator when yielding data obtained asynchronously. For details, see [Stream Data](stream-data.md){.internal-link}.
 
